**Summary:**
The paper proposes a framework for program synthesis guided RL that is applicable to partially observable environments. There 3 core components of the proposed approach:
 i) halluncinator - a generative world model approximating p(state | observation) which is pre-trained on the world; 
ii) synthesizer - a program synthesizer based on a MaxSAT solver that can generate programs reaching a desired goal from hallucinated states;
iii) executor - a modular neural network that is trained to execute the synthesized programs.
The authors demonstrate the capabilities of the proposed framework on 3 problems (2D-craft, box-world, ant-craft) and report better learning performance then other well established methods.
